<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mavia was a queen of the Arab Tanukhids in the later 4th century CE who led a revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the 370s. Her forces ravaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicia">Phoenicia</a> and defeated Roman troops, until the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> accepted her demand that an Arab hermit named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a> be made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of her people. Her troops later helped defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople">Battle of Adrianople</a>.</p></div>
